# rBrowser for Homebrew

The Homebrew tap of [rBrowser](https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@), a development browser that
shows every breakpoint of a site at once: a cask for macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel) and a formula
for Linux (x86-64).

```bash
# macOS
brew install --cask @OWNER@/rbrowser/rbrowser
# Linux
brew install @OWNER@/rbrowser/rbrowser
```

`brew upgrade rbrowser` brings the next release; rBrowser installed through Homebrew does not
replace itself. The macOS app is signed ad hoc, not notarised: macOS asks once before its first
start.

Current version: @VERSION@. The cask and the formula are written by the release workflow of
[@REPOSITORY@](https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@) with every release - issues and changes go there,
not here. The handbook's installation page:
<https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@/wiki/installation>.
